thread:
alex: Opening a PR to adjust structured output examples for tool-calling + graceful fallbacks. Main goal: show an example that has a union array (items can be string|object) and a compact parse fallback. PR at <https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1287|#1287>.

maya: thanks — can you paste the minimal example here? i'll wire up the SDK snippet after we agree on shape.

alex: sure, gist of the example:

```
// model prompt expects a JSON response with `actions` array where items are either strings or objects
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "actions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "oneOf": [
          { "type": "string" },
          { "type": "object", "properties": { "name": { "type": "string" }, "params": { "type": "object" } }, "required": ["name"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["actions"]
}
```

alex: Plan: 1) docs example w/ prompt + jsonschema, 2) SDK snippet demonstrating `parseWithFallback` behavior, 3) short note about preferring compact envelopes for low-latency callers.

kevin: Link fixes: the "function calling guide" page currently points to the old `invoke` page. i'll submit a tiny patch in the PR to update anchors. :+1:

_docs-bot: PR opened by alex: <https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1287|#1287> — status: draft. Reviewers: @maya, @kevin._

eva: small UX nit — can we show the compact envelope example that looks like `{"a":["foo",{"name":"bar"}]}`? that inline example trips our parser tests. we should show both canonical and compact forms.

sandeep: also add a note about scorer/rerankers: they expect consistent tokenization-friendly keys (no spaces) — we've had regressions where teams used "Action Name" and it broke regex-based routing.

maya: i'll draft the SDK snippet. proposal:

```
// JS SDK sketch
const resp = await redwood.infer.call({ prompt, schema: mySchema })
const parsed = parseWithFallback(resp.text, mySchema, {
  compactFallback: true,
  stripOuterText: true
})
```

maya: i'll push the snippet to the PR and wire the docs links. anyone want to take a quick look at wording before i convert to final copy?

kevin: i'll review the anchor fixes + run link checker. also will add a one-line migration note for Dedicated customers who may need to pin older model variants for compatibility.

alex: awesome — if we can get reviews in the next 24h i'll convert to ready-for-review. tagging @docs for visibility. thanks all :rocket:
